            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "ydFtF",
              "name": "Field",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "VYsAf",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "GENUI IN PRODUCTION: HOW GENUI AND A2UI ",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "GENUI IN PRODUCTION: HOW GENUI AND A2UI CHANGE MOBILE APPS"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "At some point, every mobile app will have to deal with generative UI. This talk walks through what changed when we shipped it: which abstractions survived contact with real users, how the design system had to bend, and where the model still needs guardrails…"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Ondřej Jirsák"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "n51G8",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "WE ARE ALL FUCKED: AN ANDROID DEVELOPER’",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "HUMANS"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "WE ARE ALL FUCKED: AN ANDROID DEVELOPER’S GUIDE TO THE POST-AI APOCALYPSE"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "AI is dominating Android development, driven by hype over reality. As organizations rush chatbot syntax into production, we are left cleaning up a dumpster fire of unscalable slop. It is time to look past the echo chamber and address our real challenge…"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Ashley Davies"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "M9IsBL",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "OPEN SESAME TO THE MONOLITH: RAIDING THE",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "OPEN SESAME TO THE MONOLITH: RAIDING THE LEGACY CAVE WITH AI AGENTS"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Every enterprise sits on a ‘Cave of Wonders’. A massive codebase packed with decades of invaluable business logic, hardened edge cases, and customer data. But it is usually locked behind outdated languages, undocumented dependencies, and crushing technical debt…"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Abdel Sghiouar"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "B7M3A",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "GEMINI ENTERPRISE IN PRACTICE: FROM SECU",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "AI"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "GEMINI ENTERPRISE IN PRACTICE: FROM SECURE ACCESS TO REAL BUSINESS IMPACT"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Gemini Enterprise brings generative AI into the workplace, but adopting it successfully requires more than just enabling a tool. In this talk, we explore how it fits into real organisational environments, focusing on secure access, identity integration and data boundaries…"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Dr Roushanak Rahmat"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "HXuCQ",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "m6b4K",
                  "name": "YOUR APP, THEIR DATA: LOCAL-FIRST WITH E",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "e78oD": {
                      "content": "OPEN SOURCE"
                    },
                    "mkN6E": {
                      "content": "YOUR APP, THEIR DATA: LOCAL-FIRST WITH EVOLU"
                    },
                    "hwoGY": {
                      "content": "Most apps store users’ data on a server and lend it back through an API. Local-first reverses that model: data lives on the user’s device first and remains under their control. The app works without a connection, and can outlive both its servers and the company behind it…"
                    },
                    "Xx7GA": {
                      "content": "Matěj Kříž"
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "HhAuK",
          "type": "ref",
          "ref": "NdYne",
          "name": "Closer",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "descendants": {
            "S84f6/oIg87": {
              "content": "BE THERE",
